Player1 is MALE. Translate only Text into Russian; preserve the five CSV columns.
Prefer natural common wording when suitable, but use male agreement when needed.

ENGLISH CSV:
ID,Speaker,Addressee,Predecessors,Text
@16,Velcealle,Player1,,"Hello again, adventurer. Our Ink Gallery welcomes you with its tales."
@23,Velcealle,Player1,,Is there anything else you'd like to know?
@48,Velcealle,Player1,,We should talk downstairs. Unless you popped in only to see how I'm doing.
@51,Velcealle,Player1,,I hope you are having a fine day.
@100,Velcealle,Player1,,"Hello, <CHARNAME>! You've seen all my books already—but perhaps you're here for one of the souvenirs?"
@17,Player1,Velcealle,@16,"So, from what I understood, by paying the fee I will be able to test myself in battles described in these books. Is that correct?"
@18,Player1,Velcealle,@16,"You said you came here from Cormyr, yes? Was it to open the Ink Gallery?"
@19,Player1,Velcealle,@16,What happens if I successfully learn from all these books?
@20,Player1,Velcealle,@16,Don't you have any problems with the Cowled Wizards? Aren't these books magic?
@21,Player1,Velcealle,@16,I would like to buy some souvenirs.
@22,Player1,Velcealle,@16,I think I'll go now.
@24,Player1,Velcealle,@23,"Yes. From what I understood, by paying the fee I will be able to test myself in battles described in these books. Is that correct?"
